cff-version: 1.2.0
title: serra
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  method it implements (Frisken 2022, listed under references).
type: software
authors:
  - name: Allen Institute for Brain Science
repository-code: https://github.com/AllenInstitute/serra
abstract: >-
  Analytical multi-material meshes from voxelized segmentations. A single pass
  over the volume produces a 2-manifold, watertight mesh per label regardless
  of how many labels are present, with vertex positions in fixed point so that
  meshes of adjacent chunks share seam vertices exactly and stitch by
  deduplication alone.
keywords:
  - meshing
  - surface nets
  - dual contouring
  - segmentation
  - connectomics
license: MIT
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      SurfaceNets for Multi-Label Segmentations with Preservation of Sharp
      Boundaries
    authors:
      - family-names: Frisken
        given-names: Sarah F.
    journal: Journal of Computer Graphics Techniques
    volume: 11
    issue: 1
    start: 34
    end: 54
    year: 2022
    notes: The method serra implements.
  - type: conference-paper
    title: >-
      Constrained Elastic Surface Nets: Generating Smooth Surfaces from Binary
      Segmented Data
    authors:
      - family-names: Gibson
        given-names: Sarah F. F.
    collection-title: >-
      Medical Image Computing and Computer-Assisted Intervention (MICCAI 1998)
    start: 888
    end: 898
    year: 1998
  - type: article
    title: Surface Simplification Using Quadric Error Metrics
    authors:
      - family-names: Garland
        given-names: Michael
      - family-names: Heckbert
        given-names: Paul S.
    collection-title: SIGGRAPH '97
    start: 209
    end: 216
    year: 1997
    notes: The simplifier behind reduction_factor / max_error.
